# Error handling

Pipeline (do not bypass):

```text
ApiException → ErrorMapper → Failure → Result<T> → FailureHandler → ErrorState → UI
```

- Data/Domain return `Result<T>` (`Success` / `Failure_`). Do not throw across layer boundaries.
- Map every new exception surface through `ErrorMapper`. No one-off `try/catch` in a presentation controller that swallows `DioException`.
- UI never switches on status codes. UI consumes `ErrorState` from `FailureHandler.handle`.
- Display via existing widgets: snackbar → `MySnackbar`, dialog → `MyDialog`, inline → `MyInlineError`, full screen / empty → `MyEmptyState` / `ErrorStateHost`.

```dart
// BAD
catch (e) { showDialog(context, e.toString()); }

// GOOD
case Failure_(failure: final failure):
  state = AsyncValue.data(current.copyWith(
    error: FailureHandler.handle(failure, onRetry: load),
  ));
```

Retry wording must match HTTP method (`network-architecture.mdc`): GET may retry via `executeWithRetry()`; POST/DELETE never auto-retry without an idempotency key.

Unauthorized: do not `context.go(AppRoutes.login)` from a controller catch. Update the session owner; `authGuardRedirect` navigates.
